# Day 5 — Git & Infrastructure Repository

## Goal

Install and configure Git on the Raspberry Pi, connect the Pi to the infrastructure repository, create initial server documentation, and prepare the repository for server configuration management.

## What I did

* Verified Git installation
* Configured Git username
* Configured Git email
* Created a temporary `Bhavvi` directory for testing
* Cloned the `Bhavvi-cloud` infrastructure repository
* Verified the repository and Git working tree
* Created infrastructure documentation
* Created server structure documentation
* Generated an Ed25519 SSH key for GitHub
* Added the public SSH key to GitHub
* Tested GitHub SSH authentication
* Changed the Git remote from HTTPS to SSH
* Prepared the initial infrastructure documentation commit

