## GitHub SSH Authentication

The HTTPS Git remote initially required username/password authentication, which failed because GitHub does not support normal password authentication for Git operations.

Generated an Ed25519 SSH key:

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -C "bhavyeshbhavye4072@gmail.com"
```

Generated:

```text
~/.ssh/id_ed25519
~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

The private key:

```text
~/.ssh/id_ed25519
```

must never be shared.

The public key:

```text
~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
```

was added to GitHub.

## GitHub SSH Test

Tested authentication:

```bash
ssh -T git@github.com
```

Successful result:

```text
Hi BhavyeshAsapu! You've successfully authenticated, but GitHub does not provide shell access.
```

This confirmed that the Raspberry Pi can authenticate with GitHub using SSH.

## Git Remote

Changed the repository remote from HTTPS to SSH:

```bash
git remote set-url origin git@github.com:BhavyeshAsapu/Bhavvi-cloud.git
```

SSH remote:

```text
git@github.com:BhavyeshAsapu/Bhavvi-cloud.git
```

